 "q-127616/selection/f536820c0c1f32ddcee3e47511bc4ad2b98d7b6d39e7a82b9ead1ac8dd939ba6" "q-127616/selection/6c487be82ba9f72e3f281c1f03c3511e1fa91134dbb3927d549211b5c0739fa3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127616" :question/id #uuid "ea055476-b8eb-519f-a665-b94bae5e3df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127616" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),\\sqrt{3},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2),0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),\\sqrt{3},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2),0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2) & \\sqrt{3} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2) & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡(t+2)-{cos}^{2}⁡(t+2)),0-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),1,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fiel